most like driving  down an interstate I mean there's an  exit here there's a little stop there as  long as you keep searching the  hinterlands of the road just to make  sure that this site really is on the  road and and and you're not missing  something else about the surrounding  area it literally is like driving down  the street you just we're just led from  from site to site okay final question I  have to say I could talk to you all day  about this it's thank you really very  interesting what would be the holy grail  for you if you could make some discovery  within the realm of possibility of  course what would it be  Wow yeah difficult question to answer I  mean I guess what I would say in to  presage my answer I would say that we've  already found so many things that I  would never have guessed that we might  find like one of the inscriptions  a site between luxor and naga hamadi out  in the western desert was an inscription  by one of the local governors around  2100 BCE during a time of civil war  talking about how he made an improvement  to that desert road because his his  enemy to the south had annexed the  desert and he refers in this inscription  it's very fragmentary he refers to  warfare and it's the only surviving  inscription that really refers to this  conflict between ancient Thebes modern  Luxor and the district or known as the  Egyptians call it just to the north and  and if somebody had said you know this  is probably out there I would have  rather doubted it and it would have been  on the last thing I would have thought  let's say to find one of the things I'm  always telling students that I would  like to find is an inscription of the  second intermediate period of the 17th  dynasty of Kings second and raw who we  know fought these this coalition of  Egyptian collaborators and foreign  invaders in the north during a time of a  week central authority we know that  second and raw died in battle and we  have a great historical inscription of  his successor kumo a-- so one of the  great things to find obviously would be  the second and rosti law or an  inscription of second and raw that's one  thing that would be would be very nice  to find well this has been very  fascinating thank you so much for being  here with us today insuring some of your  work all you're welcome thank you again  for the invitation for more information  about professor Darnell and his work  please visit our website at Yale edu  backslash Macmillan report be sure to  join us again for another episode of the  Macmillan report made possible through  funding from the Whitney and Betty  Macmillan Center for International and  area studies at Yale
 

